# GitHub's language bar is computed by Linguist, which counts only the files it
# classifies as `programming` or `markup`.
# This repo's substance is Markdown, which Linguist classifies as `prose` and leaves out.
# That left `assets/how-it-works.html` as the largest counted file, so GitHub called
# this an HTML project.
#
# `assets/` holds illustrations and one standalone explainer page. None of it is source.
assets/* linguist-documentation=true
